# Domoticz-LUAlert: technical settings.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" in the same directory as plugin.py and remove the "#" of the lines you want to change.
# Everything is optional: without a .env the plugin uses the values shown here. Changes take effect when the
# hardware is restarted (Setup > Hardware > the plugin > Update, or restart Domoticz). A variable of the same name in
# the environment of the Domoticz service wins over this file. A mistyped name is reported in the Domoticz log.

# The dataset that lists the alert files. https only.
# LU_DATASET_URL=https://data.public.lu/api/1/datasets/67aca67bcaea3ae62308114f/

# Further hosts alert files may be downloaded from, comma separated. The plugin only requests files from the host of
# the dataset and from other hosts of its domain (*.public.lu); add a host here only if the portal moved its files.
# LU_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# How many of the newest files of the dataset are read (10-500). Only the first poll after a start reads them all;
# later polls read only new files.
# LU_MAX_RESOURCES=100

# Seconds to wait for an answer of the portal (3-60).
# LU_HTTP_TIMEOUT=10

# How many "Alert n" devices are created (1-10). More than 3 are rarely useful: the counters always count all alerts.
# LU_ALERT_DEVICES=3

# An alert without an end time is shown for this many days after it was sent (1-365).
# LU_STALE_DAYS=10

# Rewrite an unchanged value this often, in seconds (30-86400), so that Domoticz' sensor time-out never marks a quiet
# sensor as dead.
# LU_REFRESH_INTERVAL=300

# 1 = the alert devices (Highest Severity, Alert 1 ...) show the start of the description after the headline and the
# end time, as far as the 200 characters of a Domoticz text allow (food recalls, for example, say in the description
# which shop sells the product). 0 = headline and end time only. Default 1.
# LU_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION=1

# 1 = also show test and exercise messages (as severity "Test", grey). Default 0: they are left out.
# LU_SHOW_TEST_ALERTS=0

# LU-Alert levels that count as test messages, comma separated. "D" is in the list because the Home Assistant
# integration this plugin follows does so; the plugin writes every test message it ignores to the log, once. If D
# turns out to be a real alert level in the feed, remove it here (then it is an Extreme alert).
# LU_TEST_LEVELS=T,TEST,D,LU-Alert Test,LU-Alert Exercise

# CAP categories whose alerts are left out, comma separated (Geo, Met, Safety, Security, Rescue, Fire, Health, Env,
# Transport, Infra, CBRNE, Other). An alert is left out only when ALL its categories are listed. Default: none.
# LU_IGNORE_CATEGORIES=
